# keur quality control — sonar-project.properties without sonar.projectKey.
#
# Why this exists: SonarQube/SonarCloud silently tolerate a malformed
# sonar-project.properties — unknown keys are ignored and missing ones fall back
# to defaults, so a typo or an omitted required key does not error, it just
# makes the analysis land in the wrong project (or not at all). Nothing else in
# the toolchain validates this file (Sonar itself does not pre-validate it, and
# there is no linter for it), so a per-commit nudge is the only early signal.
#
# HOW (absence engine): the rule fires when NO line declares `sonar.projectKey`.
# `content_contains: sonar` is a cheap pre-filter so only Sonar property files
# are read. Targeted by exact filename so it never touches unrelated .properties.
#
# WARN, not block: a missing key is a config smell caught best early, but a repo
# may legitimately pass the key via CI (-Dsonar.projectKey=...) instead of the
# file; blocking would be wrong there. @see docs/rules-authoring.md
id: SONAR-001
ilities: [traceability]
maturity: 3
title: sonar-project.properties missing sonar.projectKey
category: quality
severity: warning
engine: absence
action: warn
confidence: 0.6
target:
  filenames: sonar-project.properties
  content_contains: sonar
patterns:
  # Fires when this appears NOWHERE: a `sonar.projectKey = <value>` assignment.
  - regex: (?m)^\s*sonar\.projectKey\s*=\s*\S
    message: "sonar-project.properties has no sonar.projectKey — the analysis has no target project and will mis-land or be skipped. Set sonar.projectKey (or pass -Dsonar.projectKey in CI)."
fix: "Add `sonar.projectKey=<org>_<repo>` to sonar-project.properties, or pass it on the scanner CLI (`-Dsonar.projectKey=...`). The key must match the project configured in SonarQube/SonarCloud."
